## Objective
- Perform authorized security assessment (client-side + server-side) of BytePlus console `workorder` functionality at `https://console.byteplus.com/workorder/list/`, testing stored XSS, cross-tenant IDOR/authz, mass assignment, file upload, and privilege escalation, then write findings to `result/`.

## Important Details
- Two disposable accounts: A = `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com` (AccountID `3000823185`), B = `testt456` (AccountID `3001021825`); Chrome DevTools pages: pageId 1 = A `https://console.byteplus.com/workorder/list/detail?id=I-2026102917080001`, pageId 2 = B `https://console.byteplus.com/workorder/list/` (isolatedContext=userB).
- API base for ticket: `/api/top/ticket/ap-southeast-1/2021-01-01/`; file API version `2022-01-01`; authorization service: `/api/top/authorization/ap-southeast-1/2021-01-01/`.
- Requests need cookie `csrfToken` in header `x-csrf-token`, `content-type: application/json; charset=UTF-8`, `credentials:'same-origin'`.
- A's open ticket: `I-2026102917080001`.
- B's tickets/conversations: `I-2026102913150002` (cid `6ae2d691379c42c3eaccc70b`), `I-2026102913150001` (cid `6ae2d6683befc2a42b5d66ad`), `I-2026102912590002` (cid `6ae2d30f379c42c3eaccc6f6`), `I-2026102912590001`, `I-2026102912580001`, `I-2026102912570001`, `I-2026080515360001`.
- Prior conversation content is server-sanitized: `onerror` stripped from `<img>`, `javascript:` href emptied; markdown `javascript:` links rendered as `<a class="link_10ec3" target="_blank">clickme</a>` with no href (safe). Prior evidence confirmed sanitizer robust.
- Rules: use test-owned data only, never probe internal/SSRF targets without authorization, don't enumerate real IDs, no duplicate testing.
- Process: decision=reset (target hash changed); current run started `2026-10-29T11:39:08Z`, Run ID `40866925694`.
- Upload file type is validated server-side by actual MIME type, not extension (text/html, image/svg+xml, application/pdf all rejected as "Unsupported file type"); only text/plain worked.
- `DownloadFile` cross-account and `SaveFile` cross-account both return `Forbidden`.
- Client uses `*ForUser` fallback APIs on AccessDenied; these were tested and also Forbidden cross-account.

## Work State
### Completed
- Cross-account `CreateTicketConversation`: B's open ticket → `Forbidden`; B's closed ticket → `RequestInvalid` "工单状态已发生变化，请刷新页面".
- Cross-account `GetTicketForUser`, `ListTicketConversationForUser` → `Forbidden`; `CreateTicketConversationForUser` blocked similarly.
- `ListTicketForUser`/`ListTicket` with injected `AccountID`/`SubmitterID` → returns only A's own tickets (7 total); `TicketID` param returns empty. Params ignored/scoped.
- `GetSensitiveConversation` with B's ConversationID+TicketID from A → `NotFound` "Entity [%!v(MISSING)] not found".
- `CommentTicket` on A ticket → `RequestInvalid` "Evaluation is prohibited because the ticket is not completed".
- `ListTicketExecutableAction` for A ticket returns only `close` and `urge`.
- File flow: `POST /2022-01-01/UploadFile` multipart field name must be `File` → returns `FileID`; `SaveFile` returns `FileID` + signed TOS URL (5-min expiry); `DownloadFile?FileID=` serves content text/plain. Confirmed A upload/download works (FileID `751ac2e0-2e38-49c5-a269-6d4cb326982e`).
- `ListAuthorization`/`ListAuthorizationForUser` for A → empty `Data`, Total 0 (no authorization objects to test IDOR).
- `GetPreSignedDownloadURL` → `InvalidActionOrVersion` (operation not deployed).
- Inspected JS: `ListTicketFlow`, `GetFieldsRecommendation`, `GetQuestionDescription` are AI endpoints requiring Copilot `SessionID`; `ref` query param base64-decoded via `atob`, used for `SourceURL`/`CustomerReferURL` but always prefixed with `location.origin` (cannot escape origin).
- Inspected `TicketCreate` upload module (`7959` in `main.7d5d0431.js`): pre-signed TOS POST with server-provided policy; no client-controlled sigInfo.
- Inspected `WorkOrderDetail`: ticket `Description` rendered via custom component `H` as plain React text (escaped), not `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.

### Active
- Searching for remaining leads in client-side XSS / authz: considering ticket `FormContent`/`Description`/`SubmitterName` rendering, `HandleTicket` arbitrary ActionKey, `ReviewTicket`/`GetTicketReviewTemplate`, and AI endpoint reflection.
- Extracting supported file types from module `19710` (`o.PI` array) was attempted; grep timed out (command exceeded 120000 ms) on large minified files.

### Blocked
- No confirmed vulnerability yet; most cross-tenant reads/writes and file IDOR are properly blocked.
- `grep`/regex over large minified JS in `/tmp/wo` can hang/timeout — use Python per-file reads with bounded search instead.
- Authorization IDOR untestable: A has zero authorization objects; guessing real IDs disallowed.
- SSRF via `SourceURL` untestable/out of scope without authorized callback or internal-target permission.

## Next Move
1. Use Python (not grep) on `/tmp/wo` modules to extract `o.PI` supported file MIME/extension list from module `19710`, then test whether any allowed type (e.g., image/png, image/jpeg) can be served with unsafe inline `Content-Type`/missing `Content-Disposition` via `DownloadFile`.
2. Test `HandleTicket` on A ticket with support-only ActionKey guesses (e.g., `reopen`, `assign`, `transfer`, `reply`) to check for vertical privilege escalation; inspect resulting response/ticket state.
3. If no new lead, inspect `FormContent` custom field rendering in `WorkOrderDetail` / shared `609.9d2bee7c.js`, then write current negative results and coverage to `result/` (endpoints, routes, testing inventory) per AGENT.md.

## Relevant Files
- `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn/aaii-aautomattionn/` — repo root.
- `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn/aaii-aautomattionn/result/` — output root for findings/evidence.
